KB0000006	tenant_acme_01	KB0000006	SSSD LDAP Provider Connection Refusal Post-Kernel Patch on mainframe-host-01	\N	Server - Kernel & OS Patch	\N	mainframe-host-01	The April 2024 kernel patch (kernel-4.18.0-553.el8) updated the firewall backend from iptables-legacy to nftables, implicitly dropping the custom 'ldap-client' firewalld zone rule allowing outbound TCP 389/636 to the AD Domain Controllers. SSSD fails to bind to the LDAP servers, resulting in 'Connection refused' errors in /var/log/sssd/sssd_<domain>.log and user lookup failures via 'id' or 'getent'. Resolution requires re-applying the persistent firewalld direct rule for outbound LDAP traffic and restarting the sssd service.	["sssd_<domain>.log shows repeated 'ldap_sasl_bind_s failed: Can't contact LDAP server' and 'Failed to connect to LDAP server: Connection refused' for ad-dc-01.corp.example.com:636", "'systemctl status sssd' reports 'Active: active (running)' but 'sssd[pid]: ; [be[CORP.EXAMPLE.COM]] [sdap_id_op_connect_done] (0x0010): Failed to connect to LDAP server'", "'getent passwd <ad_user>' hangs for 30 seconds then returns 'No such user' while local /etc/passwd entries resolve instantly", "tcpdump -i bond0 -nn port 636 shows SYN packets leaving mainframe-host-01 with no SYN-ACK return, confirming host-level egress block"]	The kernel-4.18.0-553.el8 RPM upgrade triggered a firewalld reload which migrated the active backend to nftables, discarding the previously configured --direct --permanent --add-rule ipv4 filter OUTPUT 0 -p tcp -d 10.10.10.0/24 --dport 636 -j ACCEPT rule required for SSSD outbound LDAPS connectivity to the AD subnet.	["ssh root@mainframe-host-01", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"firewall-cmd --permanent --direct --add-rule ipv4 filter OUTPUT 0 -p tcp -d 10.10.10.0/24 --dport 389 -j ACCEPT && firewall-cmd --permanent --direct --add-rule ipv4 filter OUTPUT 0 -p tcp -d 10.10.10.0/24 --dport 636 -j ACCEPT\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"firewall-cmd --reload\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"systemctl restart sssd\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"id ad_admin_user && getent group 'Domain Admins' && tail -20 /var/log/sssd/sssd_CORP.EXAMPLE.COM.log | grep -E 'Connected|Authenticated'\\""]	10	["INC0000041", "INC0000042", "INC0000043", "INC0000044", "INC0000045", "INC0000046", "INC0000047", "INC0000048", "INC0000049", "INC0000050"]	🤖 NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B Knowledge Agent	NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B / Meta Llama 3.3 70B (NIM)	0	1	5	f	1	2026-08-01 09:40:26.198	2026-08-01 09:48:18.403
