b2a798bd-b1b0-4619-aeb2-827ed8f88e5c	tenant_acme_01	KB0000013	Troubleshooting & SOP: Active Directory LDAP Sync Failure	# Master SOP: Nexacore Application Service Recovery\n\n## Overview\nThis Standard Operating Procedure outlines the comprehensive steps to diagnose, recover, and validate the Nexacore Application when it crashes or goes offline. The Nexacore application is a lightweight Python-based HTTP web portal serving UI assets. \n\n## Target System Details\n- **Hostname**: `<server_name>` (e.g., WorkerNode1HL)\n- **Application Path**: `/opt/nexacore-app/nexacore_app.py`\n- **Log File Path**: `/opt/nexacore-app/nexacore.log`\n- **Port**: `8080`\n- **Service Type**: Background Python Process (nohup)\n\n## Prerequisites\n- SSH access to the target node as the `root` user.\n- *(Note: Replace `<server_name>` in all following commands with the actual hostname or IP address of the affected server. If passwordless SSH is not configured, supply the password when prompted. For WorkerNode1HL, the password is typically `root123`)*.\n\n---\n\n## Recovery Steps\n\n### 1. Verify Application Process State\nCheck if the Nexacore process has crashed and is no longer running on the target server.\n```bash\nssh root@<server_name> "ps aux | grep -i nexacore | grep -v grep"\n```\n- **If a process is returned**: The process is running but might be hung. You may need to kill it using `ssh root@<server_name> "kill -9 <PID>"` before restarting.\n- **If no process is returned**: The application has crashed and requires a restart.\n\n### 2. Check Application Logs for Crash Reasons (Optional)\nBefore restarting, inspect the tail of the log file to identify why the application failed.\n```bash\nssh root@<server_name> "tail -n 50 /opt/nexacore-app/nexacore.log"\n```\n- Look for Python tracebacks, OOM (Out of Memory) kills, or port binding errors.\n\n### 3. Restart the Application\nRestart the Python-based HTTP server in the background, ensuring output is redirected to the application log.\n```bash\nssh root@<server_name> "nohup python3 /opt/nexacore-app/nexacore_app.py >> /opt/nexacore-app/nexacore.log 2>&1 &"\n```\n\n### 4. Verify Process is Running\nConfirm the process has successfully started and obtained a new PID.\n```bash\nssh root@<server_name> "ps aux | grep -i nexacore | grep -v grep"\n```\n\n### 5. Validate Local Port Binding\nEnsure the application is actively listening on port 8080 locally.\n```bash\nssh root@<server_name> "ss -tulpn | grep 8080"\n```\n\n### 6. Validate Application HTTP Response\nTest the HTTP endpoint directly from the node to confirm it is serving requests.\n```bash\nssh root@<server_name> "curl -I http://127.0.0.1:8080"\n```\n- You should receive an `HTTP/1.0 200 OK` or similar successful response.	User Error - Training Provided	\N	postgres-prod-01	Standard Operating Procedure to diagnose and resolve Active Directory LDAP Sync Failure service issues.	["Service Active Directory LDAP Sync Failure reported degraded state", "Connection timeouts or refused connections in logs."]	Improper configuration settings, corrupted state files, or service crash due to memory pressure.	["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"ps aux | grep Active\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"journalctl -n 50\\""]	10	["INC0000063", "INC0000064", "INC0000065", "INC0000066", "INC0000075", "INC0000076", "INC0000077", "INC0000067", "INC0000068", "INC0000069"]	🤖 NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B Knowledge Agent	NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B / Meta Llama 3.3 70B (NIM)	0	1	5	t	1	2026-08-01 10:07:25.934	2026-08-01 21:29:07.298
