000066", "INC0000067", "INC0000068", "INC0000069", "INC0000070"], "workNotesAnalyzedCount": 10}, {"id": "KB0000007", "title": "Troubleshooting & SOP: Email Gateway Outbound Mail Queue Backlog", "author": "🤖 NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B Knowledge Agent", "number": "KB0000007", "summary": "Standard Operating Procedure to diagnose and resolve Email Gateway Outbound Mail Queue Backlog service issues.", "category": "Application - Code & SSO Fix", "symptoms": ["Service Email Gateway Outbound Mail Queue Backlog reported degraded state", "Connection timeouts or refused connections in logs."], "createdAt": "2026-08-01T09:41:24.980Z", "modelUsed": "NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B / Meta Llama 3.3 70B (NIM)", "rootCause": "Improper configuration settings, corrupted state files, or service crash due to memory pressure.", "viewCount": 1, "helpfulCount": 0, "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Log in to the target system and verify service process status: 'ps aux | grep Email' or systemctl status.\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Inspect logs using journalctl or logs in /var/log/ to identify specific errors.\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Restart the affected service process and verify it binds successfully to its network port.\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Confirm the service state remains healthy and operational metrics return to baseline.\\""], "configurationItem": "postgres-prod-01", "sourceIncidentIds": ["INC0000051", "INC0000052", "INC0000053", "INC0000054", "INC0000055", "INC0000056", "INC0000057", "INC0000058", "INC0000059", "INC0000060"], "workNotesAnalyzedCount": 10}, {"id": "KB0000006", "title": "SSSD LDAP Provider Connection Refusal Post-Kernel Patch on mainframe-host-01", "author": "🤖 NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B Knowledge Agent", "number": "KB0000006", "summary": "The April 2024 kernel patch (kernel-4.18.0-553.el8) updated the firewall backend from iptables-legacy to nftables, implicitly dropping the custom 'ldap-client' firewalld zone rule allowing outbound TCP 389/636 to the AD Domain Controllers. SSSD fails to bind to the LDAP servers, resulting in 'Connection refused' errors in /var/log/sssd/sssd_<domain>.log and user lookup failures via 'id' or 'getent'. Resolution requires re-applying the persistent firewalld direct rule for outbound LDAP traffic and restarting the sssd service.", "category": "Server - Kernel & OS Patch", "symptoms": ["sssd_<domain>.log shows repeated 'ldap_sasl_bind_s failed: Can't contact LDAP server' and 'Failed to connect to LDAP server: Connection refused' for ad-dc-01.corp.example.com:636", "'systemctl status sssd' reports 'Active: active (running)' but 'sssd[pid]: ; [be[CORP.EXAMPLE.COM]] [sdap_id_op_connect_done] (0x0010): Failed to connect to LDAP server'", "'getent passwd <ad_user>' hangs for 30 seconds then returns 'No such user' while local /etc/passwd entries resolve instantly", "tcpdump -i bond0 -nn port 636 shows SYN packets leaving mainframe-host-01 with no SYN-ACK return, confirming host-level egress block"], "createdAt": "2026-08-01T09:40:26.198Z", "modelUsed": "NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B / Meta Llama 3.3 70B (NIM)", "rootCause": "The kernel-4.18.0-553.el8 RPM upgrade triggered a firewalld reload which migrated the active backend to nftables, discarding the previously configured --direct --permanent --add-rule ipv4 filter OUTPUT 0 -p tcp -d 10.10.10.0/24 --dport 636 -j ACCEPT rule required for SSSD outbound LDAPS connectivity to the AD subnet.", "viewCount": 1, "helpfulCount": 0, "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@mainframe-host-01", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"firewall-cmd --permanent --direct --add-rule ipv4 filter OUTPUT 0 -p tcp -d 10.10.10.0/24 --dport 389 -j ACCEPT && firewall-cmd --permanent --direct --add-rule ipv4 filter OUTPUT 0 -p tcp -d 10.10.10.0/24 --dport 636 -j ACCEPT\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"firewall-cmd --reload\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"systemctl restart sssd\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"id ad_admin_user && getent group 'Domain Admins' && tail -20 /var/log/sssd/sssd_CORP.EXAMPLE.COM.log | grep -E 'Connected|Authenticated'\\""], "configurationItem": "mainframe-host-01", "sourceIncidentIds": ["INC0000041", "INC0000042", "INC0000043", "INC0000044", "INC0000045", "INC0000046", "INC0000047", "INC0000048", "INC0000049", "INC0000050"], "workNotesAnalyzedCount": 10}, {"id": "KB0000005", "title": "Troubleshooting & SOP: Okta MFA Webhook Delivery Timeout", "author": "🤖 NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B Knowledge Agent", "number": "KB0000005", "summary": "Standard Operating Procedure to diagnose and resolve Okta MFA Webhook Delivery Timeout service issues.", "category": "User Error - Training Provided", "symptoms": ["Service Okta MFA Webhook Delivery Timeout reported degraded state", "Connection timeouts or refused connections in logs."], "createdAt": "2026-08-01T09:39:43.388Z", "modelUsed": "NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B / Meta Llama 3.3 70B (NIM)", "rootCause": "Improper configuration settings, corrupted state files, or service crash due to memory pressure.", "viewCount": 1, "helpfulCount": 0, "resolutionSteps": ["ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Log in to the target system and verify service process status: 'ps aux | grep Okta' or systemctl status.\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Inspect logs using journalctl or logs in /var/log/ to identify specific errors.\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Restart the affected service process and verify it binds successfully to its network port.\\"", "ssh root@192.168.100.101 \\"Confirm the service state remains healthy and operational metrics return to baseline.\\""], "configurationItem": "mainframe-host-01", "sourceIncidentIds": ["INC0000031", "INC0000032", "INC0000033", "INC0000034", "INC0000035", "INC0000036", "INC0000037", "INC0000038", "INC0000039", "INC0000040"], "workNotesAnalyzedCount": 10}, {"id": "KB0000003", "title": "Troubleshooting & SOP: Unix Kernel Panic on Mainframe Host 01", "author": "🤖 NVIDIA Nemotron 3 550B Knowledge Agent", "number": "KB0000003", "summary": "Standard Operating Procedure 